# Product schemas

Master model: `backend/models/Product.js`.

- `subCategory`: `mongoose.Schema.Types.Mixed` — string **or** array of strings (e.g. `"Fossil, Tissot"` or `["Fossil", "Tissot"]`). Never change this to a strict String-only type.
- `isActive`: boolean — `true` live, `false` hidden from store.
- `price`: number (selling price).
- `originalPrice`: number (MRP).
- `discountPercent`: number 0–100.
- `stock`: number.

Secondary collections under `backend/models/product/`: `watch.model.js`, `watchNew.model.js`, `menModel.js`, `womenModel.js`, `accessory.model.js`, `lens.model.js`, `shoes.model.js`, `menTshirt.model.js`. All `subCategory` fields stay `Mixed`.

When updating products in `admin.controller.js`, sync `isActive`, `price`, `stock`, and `subCategory` to **both** `Product` and every relevant secondary collection.
